  "landfallEstimate": "Movement towards Andhra Pradesh coast",
  "rawBulletin": "India Meteorological Department\n(Ministry of Earth Sciences)\nNATIONAL BULLETIN NO. 5 (BOB/10/2026)\nTIME OF ISSUE:0230 HOURS IST DATED:16.11.2026\nFROM: INDIA METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (FAX NO. 24643965/24699216/24623220)\nTO: CONTROL ROOM, NDM, MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS (FAX.NO. 23093750)\nCONTROL ROOM NDMA (FAX.NO. 26701729)\nCABINET SECRETARIAT (FAX.NO.23012284, 23018638)\nPS TO HON\u2019BLE MINISTER FOR S & T AND EARTH SCIENCES (FAX NO.23316745)\nSECRETARY, MOES (FAX NO. 24629777)\nH.Q. (INTEGRATED DEFENCE STAFF AND CDS) (FAX NO. 23005137/23005147)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, DOORDARSHAN (23385843)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, AIR (23421105, 23421219)\nPIB MOES (FAX NO. 23389042)\nUNI (FAX NO. 23355841)\nD.G. NATIONAL DISASTER RESPONSE FORCE (NDRF) (FAX NO. 26105912, 2436 3260)\nDIRECTOR, PUNCTUALITY, INDIAN RAILWAYS (FAX NO. 23388503)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDAMAN & NICOBAR ISLANDS (FAX NO. 03192-232656)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDHRA PRADESH (FAX NO. 0863-2441029)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ODISHA (FAX NO. 0674-2536660)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT OF TELANGANA (FAX NO 040-23455340)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF TAMIL NADU (FAX NO. 044-25672304)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF PUDUCHERRY (FAX NO. 0413-2334145)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF CHHATTISGARH (FAX NO. 0771-2221206)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF JHARKHAND (FAX NO. 0651-2400255)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF WEST BENGAL (FAX NO. 033-22144328)\nSub: Deep Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal [Pre Cyclone Watch\nfor Andhra Pradesh & adjoining South Odisha coast Yellow Message]\nThe Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal moved north-northwestwards with\nthe speed of 08 kmph during past 06 hours, intensified into Deep Depression and lay centered at 2330\nhours IST of yesterday, the 15th November, 2026 over the same region, near Latitude 10.6\u00b0N and\nLongitude 86.7\u00b0E, about 640 km east-northeast of Trincomalee (Sri Lanka), 670km west of Sri Vijaya\nPuram (Andaman & Nicobar Islands), 760 km east-southeast of Chennai (Tamil Nadu), 870 km south-\nsoutheast of Visakhapatnam (Andhra Pradesh) and 980 km south-southeast of Gopalpur (Odisha).\nIt is very likely to continue to move north-northwestwards, intensify further into a Cyclonic Storm over the\ncentral parts of south & adjoining westcentral Bay of Bengal in the evening of 16th November and into a\nSevere Cyclonic Storm over westcentral Bay of Bengal in the evening of 17th November, 2026.\nThereafter, it is likely to intensify further and move northwestwards towards Andhra Pradesh coast during\nsubsequent 2 days.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(IST) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n15.11.26/2330 10.6/86.7 50-60 gusting to 70 Deep Depression\n16.11.26/0530 11.0/86.6 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n16.11.26/1130 11.4/86.5 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n16.11.26/1730 11.8/86.4 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n16.11.26/2330 12.2/86.3 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/1130 12.9/86.2 80-90 gusting to 100 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/2330 13.4/85.9 90-100 gusting to 110 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/1130 13.9/85.2 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/2330 14.3/84.3 110-120 gusting to 130 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/1130 14.7/83.4 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\nWarnings:\n(i) Rainfall Warning:\nAndaman & Nicobar Islands: Light to moderate rainfall at most places is very likely during 15th to 17th\nNovember.\nTamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at\nisolated places is very likely over North Tamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal on 17th & 20th with heavy to\nvery heavy rainfall at isolated places on 18th & 19th November.\nCoastal Andhra Pradesh: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at isolated places\nis very likely on 18th, light to moderate rainfall at most places with heavy to very heavy rainfall at a few\nplaces over c",
